  "How many neighbors make a decision?": "<style>@media(min-width:801px) and (max-height:780px){.public-quorum .sim canvas{height:28vh;min-height:200px}.public-quorum>.footnote{font-size:15px;margin-top:12px}}</style><div class=\"public-quorum\"><div class=\"sim-heading\"><h2>How many neighbors<br>make a decision?</h2><p class=\"lead\">A colony needs a new home.</p></div><div class=\"sim\"><canvas id=\"quorumCanvas\" width=\"1000\" height=\"300\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Scouts inspect two candidate nests. Reaching a local threshold starts transport.\">Scouts compare two nests. Read their numbers and the decision below.</canvas><div class=\"controls\"><button id=\"quorumPlay\">Start scouts</button><button id=\"quorumStep\">One assessment</button><button id=\"quorumReset\">New search</button><label for=\"threshold\">Threshold <output id=\"thresholdValue\">8</output><input id=\"threshold\" type=\"range\" min=\"3\" max=\"12\" value=\"8\"></label></div><p class=\"sim-status\" id=\"quorumStatus\">Near / exposed: 0 · Far / sheltered: 0 · Searching</p></div><p class=\"footnote\">Toy model inspired by <i>Temnothorax</i> nest choice. Counts and thresholds are invented for teaching; not a local-species claim.</p><p class=\"footnote\"><a href=\"https://pratt.lab.asu.edu/videos\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Watch actual nest-search recruitment &amp; nestmate transport ↗</a> · Stephen Pratt / Arizona State University · internet needed</p></div>",
  "Living ladders": "<div class=\"example-switch ladder-switch\"><div class=\"view-choices\" role=\"group\" aria-label=\"Choose an army-ant field photograph or research film\"><button data-view=\"ladderField\" aria-controls=\"ladderField\" aria-pressed=\"true\">Living bridge</button><button data-view=\"ladderResearch\" aria-controls=\"ladderResearch\" aria-pressed=\"false\">Research film</button></div><div id=\"ladderField\" class=\"example-panel\"><div class=\"film-layout field-ladder\"><div><h2 id=\"title-31\">Living ladders</h2><p class=\"lead\">Workers link their bodies.<br>Other ants cross the gap.</p><p class=\"watch-cue\">A structure made<br>of the workers themselves.</p></div><figure class=\"real-image ladder-photo\"><img src=\"site/ants/wild-bridge.jpg\" alt=\"Eciton burchellii army ants link legs and bodies to form a living bridge\"><figcaption><i>Eciton burchellii</i> · captive colony, California Academy of Sciences<br><a href=\"https://www.alexanderwild.com/Ants/Making-a-Living/Army-Ants/i-kNNDWCV\">© Alex Wild · used with permission</a></figcaption></figure></div><p class=\"footnote\">Living bridge photographed in a captive colony. The research film shows a different structure: a scaffold on a slope.</p></div><div id=\"ladderResearch\" class=\"example-panel\" hidden><div class=\"film-layout\"><div><h2>Living ladders</h2><p class=\"lead\">Some ants become<br>the structure.</p><p class=\"watch-cue\">Watch the lower panel.<br>Which ants stop moving?</p></div><figure><video id=\"scaffoldVideo\" controls muted playsinline preload=\"none\" aria-label=\"Research timelapse of Eciton burchellii ants assembling scaffolds at 50 and 90 degree slopes\"><source src=\"https://www.uni-konstanz.de/fileadmin/pi/fileserver/2021_EXTRA/learning_about_system_stability_from_ants_image_matthew_lutz_video_matthew_lutz_chris_reid_simon_garnier_and_iain_couzin.mp4\" type=\"video/mp4\"><track kind=\"captions\" src=\"site/ants/scaffolds.vtt\" srclang=\"en\" label=\"English description\" default></video><figcaption>Internet needed · 15-second research timelapse · 40× speed · <i>Eciton burchellii</i><br><a href=\"https://www.eurekalert.org/news-releases/722631\">Lutz, Reid, Garnier & Couzin / University of Konstanz</a></figcaption></figure></div><p class=\"footnote\">Researchers call these “scaffolds.” Stationary ants provide footholds on a slope. A wider-world example.</p></div></div>",
  "Image &amp; film credits 1": "<h2>Image &amp; film credits <span class=\"credit-page\">1</span></h2><div class=\"source-columns media-columns\"><div><p class=\"credit-item\"><a href=\"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Closeup_on_honeypot_ants_(Myrmecocystus_mimicus)_at_Oakland_Zoo.jpg\">Closeup on honeypot ants (Myrmecocystus mimicus) at Oakland Zoo.jpg</a><br>Derrick Coetzee (User:Dcoetzee)<br><a href=\"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Closeup_on_honeypot_ants_(Myrmecocystus_mimicus)_at_Oakland_Zoo.jpg\">CC0</a></p><p class=\"credit-item\"><a href=\"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Mount_Shasta,_Lake_Siskiyou,_SW_view.jpg\">Mount Shasta, Lake Siskiyou, SW view.jpg</a><br>Radomianin<br><a href=\"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Mount_Shasta,_Lake_Siskiyou,_SW_view.jpg\">CC BY-SA 4.0</a></p><p class=\"credit-item\"><a href=\"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Northern_Flicker_(red-shafted).jpg\">Northern Flicker (red-shafted).jpg</a><br>Wildreturn<br><a href=\"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Northern_Flicker_(red-shafted).jpg\">CC BY 2.0</a></p></div><div><p class=\"credit-item\"><a href=\"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Trillium_ovatum_1290.JPG\">Trillium ovatum 1290.JPG</a><br>Walter Siegmund (talk)<br><a href=\"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Trillium_ovatum_1290.JPG\">CC BY-SA 3.0</a></p><p class=\"credit-item\"><a href=\"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Ants_collecting_honeydew_drops_01.jpg\">Ants collecting honeydew drops 01.jpg</a><br>Hexafluoride<br><a href=\"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Ants_collecting_honeydew_drops_01.jpg\">CC BY-SA 4.0</a></p><p class=\"credit-item\"><a href=\"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Leafcutter_ants.webm\">Leafcutter ants.webm</a><br>Filo gèn&#x27;<br><a href=\"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Leafcutter_ants.webm\">CC BY-SA 4.0</a></p></div></div>",
